== Graphics Mods (Enhanced)

More demanding visual enhancements for a fully modded experience.

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/3486")[*Starfield HD Reworked Project*]

High-resolution texture overhaul of environments, characters, and effects, faithful to the vanilla art style. The headline graphics upgrade for this wave.

- *Author:* HalkHogan
- *Version:* 1.0-fix (updated 2023-09-23)
- *Dependencies:* None (requires `bInvalidateOlderFiles=1` from setup)
- *System Impact:* Performance — recommend a 6 GB+ VRAM GPU

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/103")[*Constellation Reshade*]

A ReShade preset tuned for Starfield, adjusting tone and color for a more cinematic image on top of the texture work above.

- *Author:* 2077v2
- *Version:* 1.2 (updated 2023-09-10)
- *Dependencies:* ReShade (installed separately)
- *System Impact:* Performance — ReShade adds a small post-processing cost
- *Notes:* Optional. Install ReShade, then place this preset and select it in-game.

=== Lighting (Creations-only — optional)

The large lighting overhaul *Real Lights Starfield* (by RabbitDoesStuff, 15,000+ hand-placed lights) is distributed only through the Bethesda Creations store, not Nexus Mods. If you want it, install it from the in-game Creations menu; it is compatible with this MO2-based list but is tracked outside it.
